<title>USA: InterContinental Life unit buys State Auto.</title>
<headline>InterContinental Life unit buys State Auto.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>InterContinental Life Corp said on Thursday that its subsidiary, Investors Life Insurance Co of Indiana purchased State Auto Life Insurance Co of Columbus, Ohio. The terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>As a result of the merger, Investors Life of Indiana's capital and surplus would be $9.3 million and assets would increase to $106.3 million.</p>
<p>InterContinental Life owns and operates three life insurance companies which have combined assets of $1.3 billion.</p>
<p>(( --New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
